<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mas'ud I of Ghazni</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Masud I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masud I was sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghaznavid-empire">Ghaznavid Empire</a>, son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a>. He failed to contain the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Turks</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a> and was decisively defeated by them at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dandanaqan">Battle of Dandanaqan</a> in 1040. The defeat opened the way for the rise of the Seljuk Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masud-i-of-ghazni.jpg" alt="Mas'ud I of Ghazni" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mas%27udIGhaznavidCoin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
